  "ingredients": [
    "1 cup all-purpose flour",
    "1 teaspoon paprika",
    "salt to taste",
    "ground black pepper to taste",
    "1 teaspoon garlic powder",
    "1 teaspoon onion powder",
    "1/2 teaspoon cayenne pepper (optional)",
    "1 (3 pound) whole chicken, cut into pieces",
    "1 quart vegetable oil for frying"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/R-lUfKbaNMZWnhX0HeK8sRbsMIs=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/8635-southern-fried-chicken-ddmfs-step1-feab05f58fd3427fb4f20504ca33a44c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8635/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine flour, paprika, salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, and cayenne in a large resealable plastic bag. Add chicken pieces to the bag; toss to coat.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/KBwDBofrBY5kBm82NLRK0-bdquQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/8635-southern-fried-chicken-mfs_step5copy-765d092403f647eba745c34cd431b501.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8635/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place floured chicken pieces on a wire rack set over a baking sheet; reserve remaining flour in the bag. Refrigerate chicken until flour looks pasty, about 45 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, heat 1 ½ inches oil in a deep fryer or 5-quart heavy pot to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/M4D2yUDxjQ-kA7A3Lb-qqXehSsw=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/8635-southern-fried-chicken-ddmfs-step4-b9a14d3b6db84ce3b092ab479525add9.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8635/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place chicken pieces back into the reserved bag of flour; toss to coat. This will help the coating cling nicely to the chicken pieces for crispier results. Preheat the oven to 200 degrees F (93 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower chicken pieces, 2 to 3 pieces at a time, carefully into the hot oil. Fry until golden, flipping once, 8 to 12 minutes. An instant-read thermometer inserted near but not touching bones should read 165 degrees F (74 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Gu3B99_MIejwPeTdfoMJr30Qxjo=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/8635-southern-fried-chicken-ddmfs-step8-41da10c18e9548eebbb837cea3878246.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8635/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Transfer to a paper towel-lined plate to drain. Keep fried chicken warm in the preheated oven while frying remaining chicken.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/EhFQNmxKhCJjK3YLjg8xZB1_lOQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/8635-southern-fried-chicken-ddmfs-step9-2933690d57d641ce8269f5e2a383bab5.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8635/step_07.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve hot and enjoy!",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/WSSoRAz2IygrMPkiJxHPbt9gqMg=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/8635-southern-fried-chicken-ddmfs_4x3-90736ab31a7a4bb59eb04e2380ccebe7.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8635/step_08.webp"
    }
  ],
